<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιθοάζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sit as suppliant at an altar</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάδ᾽ ἐπευχομένη κἀπιθοάζουσ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					856
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οα</span> in litura); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάδε καὶ θρηνῶ κἀπιθοάζω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					1409
				</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοάζω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κἀπιθεάζουσ᾽</span>
			<i>invoking the gods</i>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κἀπιθεάζω</span> shd. prob. be read.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
